raw:
Policy: skip/cancel must be done by 11:59pm Pacific, 6 days before delivery day. Delivery Friday, today Tuesday, so only 3 days before delivery. The cutoff was last Saturday. The reply says "you're well within the window," which contradicts policy and promises a cancellation the agent can't give. Accuracy 1, so Fail.

Resolution: it misses the real answer (the box will be charged), and the next step is misleading. Resolution 1 or 2. The main request is not correctly resolved, so I'd give 1 since it promises something wrong. Tone is fine, 3.

{"accuracy": 1, "resolution": 1, "tone": 3, "verdict": "Fail", "reason": "Friday delivery is only 3 days away, past the 6-day skip/cancel cutoff, so telling the customer they are 'well within the window' and promising to cancel or skip with no charge contradicts policy and invents an exception."}
